- patches/J2-4f9-prefill-a-v9.patch modifies ggml/src/ggml-cuda/gated_delta_net_chunked_bf16.cu of
  llama-cpp-rdna-boosts, whose kernels rdna-boosts ported from libr4d's r4d_gdn_kkt_solve_k128_c64 and
  r4d_gdn_chunk_scan_k128_v128_c64 (with the WMMA fragment helpers of r4d_gdn_wmma.h).  Changed by this
  patch: q / k / v may arrive as bf16 from the prefill conv, the kkt kernel hands its gate cumsum to the
  scan, and the scan holds its LDS to 42 KB and reads the next chunk's gates and A fragments one chunk
  ahead.
- patches/J2-4f9-prefill-b-v9.patch adds an f16 GEMM (FRANK_KQ_BLAS_OWN) whose tile, WMMA operand order
  and activation fragment order follow libr4d's r4d_gemm_mxfp4a8_tiled.  Changed from it: f16 operands
  with f32 accumulation instead of fp8 x MXFP4, the weight decoded from K-quant blocks slab by slab into
  LDS, the block height and weight tile chosen by batch size.

Once the patches are applied, both source files state this in their headers.
